<h2 id="ha-ctrl-001-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Use fixtures for valid 0, negative readings, unknown, unavailable, assumed state, absent attribute and explicit null; compare both visible text and accessible names.
2. Hold a value constant while reports arrive, and stop reports under a documented cadence. Only the second case may become stale. Test integrations that do not rewrite unchanged states.
3. Remove and restore the entity during an open details view. Preserve identity and focus; do not resurrect an older value as current.
4. Check long names, native locale, a repeated daylight-saving hour, dark mode and forced colours. Record source review separately from connected-device verification.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

